  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 9.8.0 - curl parity release: tested against curl's own test suite\n\nPARITY: tests/CurlDotNet.CurlSuite replays 1,092 HTTP tests from curl's own suite against a local stub\n   server and compares the exact bytes on the wire. 607 of 620 runnable tests pass (97.9%), 216 byte-exact;\n   the 13 remaining are documented in known-failures.txt (HttpClient CONNECT/NTLM, .NET URI rules, no ~/.curlrc).\nNEW: complete curl 8.7.1 option table; combined short flags (-sSL), attached values (-ofile, -m10), --long=value,\n   --url, --next, multiple URLs, {a,b}/[1-3] globbing with #1 in -o, -K config files, --variable, .netrc, -G, -T,\n   -z, -r multi-ranges, --oauth2-bearer, --http1.0/1.1/2, --request-target, --connect-to, --resolve, --path-as-is\nNEW: curl flavors - CurlFlavor.Auto/Posix/WindowsCmd/PowerShell/InvokeWebRequest. Commands pasted from bash,\n   Windows CMD, PowerShell or PowerShell's Invoke-WebRequest alias are detected and read with that shell's rules\n   (Curl.ExecuteAsync(cmd, CurlFlavor.PowerShell), Curl.DefaultFlavor, Curl.DetectFlavor)\nNEW: cookie engine (-b FILE, -c JAR, -j, Netscape jars), curl-exact multipart (-F ;type= ;filename= <file --form-string),\n   -D/-J/--output-dir/--create-dirs/--no-clobber/-R/-C -, every -w variable incl. %{json}, --retry family with\n   Retry-After, --limit-rate/--speed-limit, --cacert/--capath/--cert/--key/--pinnedpubkey/--tlsv1.x (.NET 5+)\nNEW: pure-C# Digest and NTLM negotiation matching curl byte for byte; --anyauth; proxy auth; Proxy-Connection,\n   preemptive proxy Basic, --noproxy/NO_PROXY, http_proxy env vars, --socks4/4a/5/5-hostname, -p CONNECT tunnels\nNEW: curl exit codes as typed exceptions (2, 3, 5-8, 18, 22, 23, 26, 28, 33, 35, 43, 47, 49, 52, 56, 60, 61, 63, 77,\n   90, 94, 100); every exception says what happened, how to fix it and links the documentation\nNEW: Curl.ExecuteAsync(CurlOptions), Curl.DefaultUserAgent (curl/8.7.1 like curl), Accept: */* default,\n   -H \"Name:\" suppression, CurlException.StandardOutput, CurlOptions.UnknownOptions/UnsupportedOptions\nNEW: full XML documentation on every public member (parameters, formats, defaults, worked examples, cross-links)\nFIX: (#45) Post/PostJson/Download helpers no longer break on quotes or spaces\nFIX: --compressed only sends Accept-Encoding when asked; -o leaves Body empty like curl; -i -o writes headers to\n   the file; -L turns POST into GET on 301/302/303 and strips Authorization across hosts; --max-redirs exact\nFIX: no hidden 30 s / 100 s timeouts; --max-time covers the body; --connect-timeout enforced; decimals accepted\nFIX: cancellation is OperationCanceledException; LibCurl returns failed results instead of throwing and honours\n   proxy/-k/redirect settings; CurlSettings Proxy/UserAgent/Cookies/OnRedirect/Progress/Retries now apply\nFIX: ParseJson is case-insensitive; AsJsonDynamic returns a real dynamic object; credentials masked in logs\nPACKAGE: net10.0 added; unused Ninject and System.CommandLine dependencies removed\nTESTS: 1,788 unit tests run offline in seconds against an in-process server (no fixed ports, no internet)\nFrameworks: netstandard2.0, net472, net48, net8.0, net9.0, net10.0\nSponsored by IronSoftware\n\nDocumentation: https://jacob-mellor.github.io/curl-dot-net/",
